1102
01:21:31,030 --> 01:21:32,890
Okay, I'm seeing darkness over there.

1103
01:21:34,790 --> 01:21:38,410
Let's just double-check this region here one last time with the scope.

1104
01:21:40,630 --> 01:21:43,170
That looks a little too dark there, also here.

1105
01:21:44,630 --> 01:21:47,190
In fact, if I don't see any enemies here, I should be okay, I guess.

1106
01:21:48,990 --> 01:21:53,670
And I don't see any, so... Yeah, we're fine.

1107
01:21:54,350 --> 01:21:57,150
That would be enemies here, if it wasn't already perfect.

1108
01:21:59,560 --> 01:22:00,660
But I am hearing an enemy.

1109
01:22:08,160 --> 01:22:09,760
Oh, this part was definitely not finished.

1110
01:22:12,980 --> 01:22:14,120
Ah, this is where I was.

1111
01:22:14,380 --> 01:22:15,320
Now I remember.

1112
01:22:15,580 --> 01:22:16,580
Yeah, look at all this.

1113
01:22:16,640 --> 01:22:17,280
Here's the party.

1114
01:22:18,140 --> 01:22:20,820
The interns, this is where they're stashing all the mobs.

1115
01:22:22,620 --> 01:22:22,980
Insanity.

1116
01:22:29,730 --> 01:22:31,610
One hitting everyone, except you.

1117
01:22:31,870 --> 01:22:34,170
You're somehow a little more resistant than the rest.

1118
01:22:43,990 --> 01:22:45,990
I should use the sword against these fools.

1119
01:22:50,730 --> 01:22:53,270
Slowly but surely, we take territory.

1120
01:22:57,570 --> 01:22:59,010
See, where did you come from?

1121
01:22:59,990 --> 01:23:00,630
Huh?

1122
01:23:01,450 --> 01:23:03,470
Did you spawn somewhere back here?

1123
01:23:05,390 --> 01:23:06,790
That's a curious one.

1124
01:23:25,920 --> 01:23:26,840
I just had a thought.

1125
01:23:29,560 --> 01:23:31,600
Regarding the food situation.

1126
01:23:33,440 --> 01:23:39,580
Maybe the reason why... or the way that... Where the hell are you coming from?

1127
01:23:39,940 --> 01:23:40,940
Hold on.

1128
01:23:42,040 --> 01:23:42,760
Where?

1129
01:23:44,760 --> 01:23:47,240
Are you spawning there or something?

1130
01:23:49,500 --> 01:23:50,300
Here?

1131
01:23:52,740 --> 01:23:54,160
Like, I don't believe it.

1132
01:23:56,360 --> 01:23:58,100
Are you falling from...

1133
01:23:58,360 --> 01:23:59,540
Upstairs, somehow?

1134
01:24:01,460 --> 01:24:02,280
Hmm.

1135
01:24:05,280 --> 01:24:07,000
Very weird.

1136
01:24:10,890 --> 01:24:11,290
Okay.

1137
01:24:13,550 --> 01:24:16,410
I was thinking, steaks, they heal for four, right?

1138
01:24:17,430 --> 01:24:22,050
I think that when you eat a steak, it's sort of... Let me point with the mouse.

1139
01:24:22,250 --> 01:24:23,310
So you have all these.

1140
01:24:23,590 --> 01:24:26,770
If you eat a steak, it's going to give you four invisible extra ones.

1141
01:24:27,490 --> 01:24:31,590
That's why it takes longer to deplete, because they have to get through those four invisible ones first.

1142
01:24:32,890 --> 01:24:38,990
And if you eat something that gives, like, for example, the cookie, it's going to give you, like, only one... I don't know if that's...

1143
01:24:39,100 --> 01:24:44,080
That's exactly how it works, but it would make sense to have a system like that.

1144
01:24:59,830 --> 01:25:02,190
Torch, torch, torch is everywhere.

1145
01:25:02,870 --> 01:25:03,990
Right, axe time.

1146
01:25:05,830 --> 01:25:07,170
Jesus, you came from upstairs.

1147
01:25:09,950 --> 01:25:11,250
Gotta clean that up too.

1148
01:25:12,410 --> 01:25:13,650
This is a problem area.

1149
01:25:21,860 --> 01:25:22,560
Give me these.

1150
01:25:22,900 --> 01:25:23,360
Give me that.

1151
01:25:23,880 --> 01:25:24,820
I'll actually do that instead.

1152
01:25:27,500 --> 01:25:31,440
I was about to say I should have brought night vision potions, but good thing I didn't.

1153
01:25:32,120 --> 01:25:33,260
That would have been really dumb.

1154
01:25:36,160 --> 01:25:37,320
I'm not done filling this.

1155
01:25:44,540 --> 01:25:45,880
Just fill it with all kinds of crap.

1156
01:25:46,100 --> 01:25:48,180
At this point, I just want to get it out of my inventory.

1157
01:25:53,820 --> 01:25:54,800
Brought two kinds of wood.

1158
01:25:55,000 --> 01:25:56,140
That is a rookie mistake.

1159
01:26:09,500 --> 01:26:10,440
Okay, let's get up here.

1160
01:26:12,800 --> 01:26:14,280
Hopefully this is just a small area.

1161
01:26:14,500 --> 01:26:15,520
It doesn't look like it.

1162
01:26:26,560 --> 01:26:36,440
I do wonder if I've chosen a mission here that is so insanely... What do you call it?

1163
01:26:37,840 --> 01:26:38,400
Big?

1164
01:26:40,240 --> 01:26:40,800
Overwhelming?

1165
01:26:40,920 --> 01:26:42,560
That it's just actually insane.

1166
01:26:44,240 --> 01:26:49,200
That if I ever finish this, that I think, in hindsight, not worth it.

1167
01:26:49,640 --> 01:26:54,000
Or that was a really dumb thing to do.

1168
01:26:55,580 --> 01:26:56,860
We'll have to see about it.

1169
01:27:02,240 --> 01:27:03,040
Yeah, okay.

1170
01:27:05,100 --> 01:27:07,080
Getting a little impatient with the creepers.

1171
01:27:09,400 --> 01:27:10,380
Plenty of light there.

1172
01:27:20,640 --> 01:27:22,160
How are you... okay, wait a minute.

1173
01:27:25,480 --> 01:27:28,480
What rules do you guys follow when it comes to spawning, huh?

1174
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:31,180
Because I don't think I get it.

1175
01:27:34,320 --> 01:27:35,180
What's happening with you?

1176
01:27:52,460 --> 01:27:53,820
Something like that.

1177
01:27:55,300 --> 01:27:56,260
Oh god.

1178
01:28:05,600 --> 01:28:06,800
One thing is for sure, though.

1179
01:28:08,500 --> 01:28:11,520
I have learned many new things doing this.

1180
01:28:12,540 --> 01:28:15,340
Not directly related to whatever it is I'm doing, right?

1181
01:28:16,260 --> 01:28:18,780
Random things are being learned.

1182
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:21,100
And that's important.

1183
01:28:23,200 --> 01:28:25,080
Where the hell are you guys coming from here?

1184
01:28:28,980 --> 01:28:30,280
And why are you here?

1185
01:28:38,310 --> 01:28:39,250
You're still alive, huh?

1186
01:28:45,790 --> 01:28:48,130
This is right below where I was just before, I think.

1187
01:28:55,260 --> 01:28:56,240
Why is there light down?

1188
01:28:56,360 --> 01:28:57,240
Oh, did I already do that?

1189
01:28:59,100 --> 01:29:01,240
This place is a little too dark, I think.

1190
01:29:01,440 --> 01:29:05,020
I've been here before, but... Shoddy job, I would say.

1191
01:29:05,840 --> 01:29:06,240
Maybe?

1192
01:29:06,480 --> 01:29:10,080
Well, I don't see any mops, so... But this is surely too dark.

1193
01:29:12,060 --> 01:29:12,460
Surely!

1194
01:29:14,700 --> 01:29:15,340
And here?

1195
01:29:24,140 --> 01:29:25,060
Okay, maybe it's fine.

1196
01:29:35,240 --> 01:29:36,760
This, though, is too dark.

1197
01:29:43,520 --> 01:29:45,100
Let's get a bird's-eye view of the place.

1198
01:29:47,980 --> 01:29:51,640
Obviously this right here needs to be... Whoa, what did it mean to fly that fast?

1199
01:29:54,100 --> 01:29:58,220
I wonder if Bane of Arthropods works on you.

1200
01:29:59,920 --> 01:30:00,600
Don't think so.

1201
01:30:02,600 --> 01:30:06,080
Not that it makes sense that it would, but you know, you never know with this game.

1202
01:30:21,540 --> 01:30:26,720
Sometimes I feel like I have so much Geschwindigkeit that I should have died, but I don't.

1203
01:30:27,680 --> 01:30:29,280
So I don't think it's all about speed.

1204
01:30:30,140 --> 01:30:31,040
There's more to it.

1205
01:30:38,380 --> 01:30:39,020
Oh yeah?

1206
01:30:41,280 --> 01:30:43,360
You came from upstate, huh?

1207
01:30:46,830 --> 01:30:47,790
Oh, here's the gang.

1208
01:30:56,880 --> 01:30:57,940
What did you just drop?

1209
01:30:58,420 --> 01:30:59,200
What kind of helmet?

1210
01:31:00,120 --> 01:31:01,560
Whoa, did you see that?

1211
01:31:03,900 --> 01:31:04,780
Oh, never mind.

1212
01:31:07,100 --> 01:31:09,400
I thought it said flight duration.

1213
01:31:10,080 --> 01:31:13,740
I thought that was an enchant flight duration, meaning I could fly longer.

1214
01:31:14,660 --> 01:31:16,680
Fuck, I totally read what I wanted to read there.

1215
01:31:18,060 --> 01:31:19,500
Damn, I'm so sad now.

1216
01:31:20,640 --> 01:31:22,120
I really thought that was real.

1217
01:31:22,880 --> 01:31:23,320
Damn.

1218
01:31:29,610 --> 01:31:33,270
I want flight duration 4 on my helmet.

1219
01:31:37,080 --> 01:31:43,180
And it would make sense too, you know, like... Wait, where the... Wait, these guys are spawning in some kind of cave down there.

1220
01:31:43,320 --> 01:31:44,320
Let's not forget about that.

1221
01:31:44,420 --> 01:31:45,180
Cave, cave, cave.

1222
01:31:45,360 --> 01:31:45,880
Go back, cave.

1223
01:31:46,640 --> 01:31:50,000
Whoa, I just accidentally hit my mouse and it slid across the mousepad.

1224
01:31:51,240 --> 01:31:53,380
That's what happens when you have a glass mousepad.

1225
01:31:54,200 --> 01:31:55,160
Things just slide.

1226
01:31:56,800 --> 01:31:57,500
Like dolphins.

1227
01:31:59,800 --> 01:32:01,300
In Fight Club.

1228
01:32:10,160 --> 01:32:10,660
Got him!

1229
01:32:14,080 --> 01:32:16,040
Master Marksman.

1230
01:32:24,960 --> 01:32:26,100
I'm trying to aim for the head.

1231
01:32:26,240 --> 01:32:27,400
I don't know if it actually does a difference.

1232
01:32:27,640 --> 01:32:28,360
Or makes a difference.

1233
01:32:30,760 --> 01:32:32,760
I am inclined to say it doesn't.

1234
01:32:33,740 --> 01:32:34,920
Because I haven't felt the difference.

1235
01:32:47,010 --> 01:32:50,010
I can't wait to test the Orphan Crusher after all this.

1236
01:32:51,150 --> 01:33:03,070
Next time I turn the Orphan Crusher on, or I just sit there and wait and let it work, it's gonna be after I have exhaustively just painstakingly gone through this.

1237
01:33:03,130 --> 01:33:06,730
I don't want to be disappointed one more time when I activate that son of a gun.

1238
01:33:07,970 --> 01:33:09,790
It needs to just work.

1239
01:33:12,410 --> 01:33:15,370
And I mean in the way Todd Howard speaks, you know?

1240
01:33:16,050 --> 01:33:17,450
That's what I... but for real, though.

1241
01:33:17,730 --> 01:33:18,350
No lies here.

1242
01:33:24,730 --> 01:33:25,130
There.

1243
01:33:26,250 --> 01:33:26,870
Oh, man.

1244
01:33:26,930 --> 01:33:27,410
Look at all this.

1245
01:33:28,050 --> 01:33:28,850
See, here's the question.

1246
01:33:28,930 --> 01:33:30,330
Am I too far from home right now?

1247
01:33:32,090 --> 01:33:33,650
I want to say I'm not.

1248
01:33:36,590 --> 01:33:37,830
But let's check the map.

1249
01:33:39,550 --> 01:33:40,970
Oh, I don't have any maps left.

1250
01:33:43,230 --> 01:33:44,570
I am north of home.

1251
01:33:45,930 --> 01:33:47,910
How much north am I from home, though?

1252
01:33:49,210 --> 01:33:49,950
That's south.

1253
01:33:53,310 --> 01:33:54,510
We can check this.

1254
01:33:57,070 --> 01:33:58,470
Let's try and go a little south.

1255
01:34:04,620 --> 01:34:14,100
Now we're definitely too much west, but as soon as we emerge... Let's see here.

1256
01:34:22,360 --> 01:34:24,400
Okay, we're going quite south right now.

1257
01:34:24,520 --> 01:34:25,320
That's a lot of south.

1258
01:34:27,920 --> 01:34:30,480
Maybe that is actually... Yeah, see, now we're up here.

1259
01:34:30,940 --> 01:34:33,200
Right now we are at the community center.

1260
01:34:33,580 --> 01:34:34,800
Community center is right up there.

1261
01:34:38,360 --> 01:34:41,360
So this is actually the hot spot for where I should be lighting.

1262
01:34:41,600 --> 01:34:42,800
So that's a good thing I'm doing it here.

1263
01:34:43,360 --> 01:34:45,180
This over here needs to be fixed too.

1264
01:34:46,240 --> 01:34:48,840
I think I definitely need to light that place I was in just now.

1265
01:34:49,780 --> 01:34:53,680
Because I think, if anything, it's right at the border of where things would spawn.

1266
01:34:56,000 --> 01:34:57,360
So maybe not further than that.

1267
01:34:57,680 --> 01:34:59,800
Because we already did go quite a distance north.

1268
01:35:01,440 --> 01:35:04,120
And let's not forget that... Okay, so 128 blocks.

1269
01:35:07,680 --> 01:35:09,200
It's like a Pythagorean, right?

1270
01:35:09,360 --> 01:35:14,820
So it's also down and then horizontal, so you have to calculate the hypotenuse of that.

1271
01:35:17,720 --> 01:35:22,940
And I don't know how far down I am, of course, but... You could calculate that, I guess.

1272
01:35:23,200 --> 01:35:24,400
Okay, so this is way too dark.

1273
01:35:24,560 --> 01:35:26,440
This is definitely a problem right here.

1274
01:35:26,600 --> 01:35:27,060
Let's fix it.

1275
01:35:29,420 --> 01:35:29,740
Yoink!

1276
01:35:29,980 --> 01:35:30,980
Ah, I thought I put it!

1277
01:35:31,360 --> 01:35:31,680
Damn.

1278
01:35:40,060 --> 01:35:41,160
What are you down there?

1279
01:35:41,280 --> 01:35:41,420
Wait.

1280
01:35:42,200 --> 01:35:43,140
Oh, it's just a zombie.

1281
01:35:45,520 --> 01:35:46,800
I thought it was a zombie villager.

1282
01:35:50,060 --> 01:35:51,360
Wait, where did you come from?

1283
01:35:51,760 --> 01:35:52,660
Oh, okay, I see dark.

1284
01:35:52,940 --> 01:35:53,720
It probably came from here.

1285
01:35:55,320 --> 01:35:55,880
That's lava.

1286
01:36:03,460 --> 01:36:04,340
Holy creeper!

1287
01:36:05,620 --> 01:36:06,060
Wow!

1288
01:36:06,480 --> 01:36:06,740
Uh-oh!

1289
01:36:06,900 --> 01:36:07,140
Uh-oh!

1290
01:36:07,380 --> 01:36:08,180
I'm in big trouble!

1291
01:36:10,600 --> 01:36:11,340
Not the children!

1292
01:36:13,860 --> 01:36:14,420
I'm dead!

1293
01:36:14,560 --> 01:36:14,820
I'm dead!

1294
01:36:16,060 --> 01:36:16,640
I'm dead.

1295
01:36:20,110 --> 01:36:21,070
Fuck this crap.

1296
01:36:23,670 --> 01:36:25,650
Way too many enemies, man.

1297
01:36:28,510 --> 01:36:30,750
The good news is we have an easy way down.

1298
01:36:32,930 --> 01:36:37,250
And the other good news is we used all our levels, so it's actually fine.

1299
01:36:40,310 --> 01:36:41,790
Levels were used beforehand.

1300
01:36:42,270 --> 01:36:44,350
I think I was level 10, if anything.

1301
01:36:47,450 --> 01:36:48,450
Yeah, it's actually not that bad.

1302
01:36:50,130 --> 01:36:51,970
See, now I kind of regret not bringing a bed.

1303
01:36:53,050 --> 01:36:53,330
Hmm.

1304
01:36:55,030 --> 01:36:55,770
Isn't that curious?

1305
01:36:57,110 --> 01:36:58,510
Ah, but wait, how am I going to get down?

1306
01:36:58,790 --> 01:36:59,910
Fuck, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

1307
01:37:00,970 --> 01:37:01,810
I can't get down.

1308
01:37:02,010 --> 01:37:03,010
I need to bring a pocket.

1309
01:37:04,590 --> 01:37:05,690
A pocket and a blanket.

1310
01:37:15,120 --> 01:37:16,980
Bucket of water, preferably.

1311
01:37:17,300 --> 01:37:18,000
There we go.

1312
01:37:22,980 --> 01:37:23,780
Let's do it.

1313
01:37:26,180 --> 01:37:27,400
That's all a man needs.

1314
01:37:28,060 --> 01:37:29,360
A bucket of water.

1315
01:37:30,660 --> 01:37:33,200
Literally, give me that and I can do anything in this game.

1316
01:37:36,180 --> 01:37:40,460
I could probably kill the dragon with just a bucket of water.

1317
01:37:41,720 --> 01:37:42,120
How?

1318
01:37:43,140 --> 01:37:43,720
I don't know.

1319
01:37:43,760 --> 01:37:44,460
It's not important how.

1320
01:37:44,600 --> 01:37:45,500
I'm just able to.

1321
01:37:49,910 --> 01:37:51,110
Yo, check this out.

1322
01:37:51,710 --> 01:37:52,790
We're gonna wait a bit here.

1323
01:37:53,010 --> 01:37:54,370
As soon as the torch goes out... There.

1324
01:37:56,210 --> 01:37:57,570
See, I took the water with me.

1325
01:37:59,650 --> 01:38:00,390
Pro place.

1326
01:38:02,570 --> 01:38:03,390
Wait, where am I now?

1327
01:38:05,690 --> 01:38:08,050
Good news is, I lit all these caves, so there's no danger.

1328
01:38:10,610 --> 01:38:12,250
I guess it's just down, isn't it?

1329
01:38:15,830 --> 01:38:16,970
Should maybe be here.

1330
01:38:18,450 --> 01:38:19,250
Seems correct.

1331
01:38:22,070 --> 01:38:23,170
Go, go, go, go, go.

1332
01:38:26,990 --> 01:38:27,430
Alrighty.

1333
01:38:29,930 --> 01:38:31,430
Let's figure out where we died.

1334
01:38:34,520 --> 01:38:39,260
I just realized this may actually be... Also, do not fly.

1335
01:38:39,260 --> 01:38:40,280
I don't have elytra.

1336
01:38:40,500 --> 01:38:40,960
Holy crap.

1337
01:38:41,100 --> 01:38:45,060
I was just about to soar straight into the concrete.

1338
01:38:45,880 --> 01:38:50,740
I think I died over here somewhere.

1339
01:38:55,800 --> 01:38:56,480
Did I?

1340
01:38:59,820 --> 01:39:00,980
Fuck, I don't remember.

1341
01:39:04,900 --> 01:39:05,520
Uh-oh.

1342
01:39:06,440 --> 01:39:08,080
Oh no, don't tell me that's where it died.

1343
01:39:12,940 --> 01:39:13,960
Wait, where's my items?

1344
01:39:17,100 --> 01:39:17,980
I can't tell!

1345
01:39:20,500 --> 01:39:21,660
I see experience there!

1346
01:39:22,040 --> 01:39:23,220
This has to be it.

1347
01:39:26,120 --> 01:39:26,960
This has to be it.

1348
01:39:31,040 --> 01:39:32,480
I just realized I don't have a weapon.

1349
01:39:42,240 --> 01:39:45,340
Don't you fucking dare exp... He's wearing my shit!

1350
01:39:45,540 --> 01:39:45,980
Look at him!

1351
01:39:46,240 --> 01:39:47,480
He has a cape on!

1352
01:39:48,820 --> 01:39:49,800
Look at that!

1353
01:39:50,880 --> 01:39:52,120
What a little bastard!

1354
01:39:54,300 --> 01:39:55,680
Nah, bro, I'm coming for you.

1355
01:39:56,760 --> 01:39:58,480
Nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah.

1356
01:39:58,600 --> 01:39:59,380
That ain't happening.

1357
01:39:59,620 --> 01:40:00,500
Not on my watch.

1358
01:40:02,620 --> 01:40:04,120
Uh... Oh, nice, I got the bow.

1359
01:40:04,200 --> 01:40:05,080
That's actually so huge.

1360
01:40:09,300 --> 01:40:11,120
Also, there's a zombie villager right there.

1361
01:40:11,780 --> 01:40:12,660
Dude, he's worried.

1362
01:40:12,780 --> 01:40:15,460
He has the whole kiddle caboodle on.

1363
01:40:17,840 --> 01:40:18,600
Thank you.

1364
01:40:19,700 --> 01:40:20,180
Unbelievable.

1365
01:40:20,380 --> 01:40:21,400
The nerve of this guy.

1366
01:40:22,120 --> 01:40:24,520
Probably the most pimped out zombie I've ever seen.

1367
01:40:26,460 --> 01:40:27,140
Look at that.

1368
01:40:27,260 --> 01:40:27,620
We're back.

1369
01:40:28,740 --> 01:40:29,420
Easy peasy.

1370
01:40:32,200 --> 01:40:32,680
Why?

1371
01:40:33,080 --> 01:40:33,560
Bastard.

1372
01:40:34,680 --> 01:40:37,420
I wasn't even close to hitting him, and he still somehow succumbed.

1373
01:40:40,970 --> 01:40:42,930
Back up, back up, back up, back up.

1374
01:40:43,630 --> 01:40:44,070
Torches.

1375
01:40:45,050 --> 01:40:45,490
Food.

1376
01:40:46,410 --> 01:40:46,850
Eat.

1377
01:40:50,510 --> 01:40:52,710
This guy really wants to bring me some rotten meat, huh?

1378
01:40:54,990 --> 01:40:57,290
Well, I'm not in the mood for rotten meat.

1379
01:41:08,700 --> 01:41:10,320
I gotta light it, I need to light it.

1380
01:41:11,580 --> 01:41:13,060
Fucking hell, there's so many enemies.

1381
01:41:14,440 --> 01:41:15,620
What is actually happening?

1382
01:41:34,040 --> 01:41:35,700
Get around like this...

1383
01:41:40,180 --> 01:41:40,980
Bounced off of him!

1384
01:41:43,660 --> 01:41:44,060
Insanity.

1385
01:41:51,600 --> 01:41:52,000
Boom!

1386
01:41:54,640 --> 01:41:55,320
There we go!

1387
01:41:57,820 --> 01:41:59,060
Man, pull up your trousers.

1388
01:42:02,480 --> 01:42:05,020
Wait, I wonder if that actually has a hitbox.

1389
01:42:05,420 --> 01:42:13,700
If he doesn't have a chest plate on and only trousers, if I hit him in the chest, will that actually not do anything for him then, wearing those trousers?

1390
01:42:14,740 --> 01:42:15,340
I wonder.

1391
01:42:18,060 --> 01:42:19,520
Let me mine this here for a sec.

1392
01:42:23,520 --> 01:42:26,420
No, no, no, no, no, no.

1393
01:42:26,760 --> 01:42:27,380
Leave me alone.

1394
01:42:31,440 --> 01:42:32,140
Keep lighting.

1395
01:42:40,440 --> 01:42:41,800
Who are you laughing at?

1396
01:42:44,800 --> 01:42:46,360
You wouldn't dare laugh at me, would you know?

1397
01:42:51,420 --> 01:42:59,720
I would say my gameplay has been exemplary, except maybe one tiny mistake, which is dying and throwing away everything I had.

1398
01:43:00,400 --> 01:43:02,800
Other than that, 10 out of 10.

1399
01:43:07,320 --> 01:43:08,400
Ah, get away from me.

1400
01:43:12,400 --> 01:43:13,620
It's tough love, my friend.

1401
01:43:13,920 --> 01:43:15,140
I'm doing it to help you.

1402
01:43:15,720 --> 01:43:16,620
You understand me?

1403
01:43:20,800 --> 01:43:21,620
Keep lighting.

1404
01:43:22,980 --> 01:43:25,120
I really like this lava right here.

1405
01:43:26,680 --> 01:43:28,780
I can't explain why, I just really do.

1406
01:43:29,280 --> 01:43:35,220
That really speaks to me on some kind of level that I find difficulty describing.

1407
01:43:37,720 --> 01:43:38,900
Makes me think of broom.

1408
01:43:43,290 --> 01:43:46,870
Which you may think is a negative thought for me right now, but it's actually kind of positive.

1409
01:43:48,370 --> 01:43:49,370
I turned it around.

1410
01:43:49,710 --> 01:43:50,110
Oh god.

1411
01:43:52,730 --> 01:43:53,750
Dodge, dodge, dodge.

1412
01:43:55,910 --> 01:43:56,410
Got him.

1413
01:44:09,610 --> 01:44:10,410
How did I miss?

1414
01:44:15,730 --> 01:44:21,110
Okay, I'm also gonna need my... Did I get all my pouches, actually?

1415
01:44:22,230 --> 01:44:22,770
I did?

1416
01:44:22,990 --> 01:44:23,750
That is incredible.

1417
01:44:38,030 --> 01:44:39,590
It'll be right as rain in no time.

1418
01:44:40,570 --> 01:44:41,270
Yeah, hit each other!

1419
01:44:41,710 --> 01:44:42,110
Idiots!

1420
01:44:55,830 --> 01:44:57,270
There you are!

1421
01:44:58,450 --> 01:44:59,330
Fixed!

1422
01:45:00,070 --> 01:45:02,930
Now, uh... Let me see here.

1423
01:45:06,650 --> 01:45:08,610
I'm gonna need you to stay.

1424
01:45:10,810 --> 01:45:11,690
Hey.

1425
01:45:21,130 --> 01:45:21,570
Sorry.

1426
01:45:21,570 --> 01:45:22,670
No, I'm sorry.

1427
01:45:24,850 --> 01:45:25,290
Mistake.

1428
01:45:25,510 --> 01:45:25,950
Mistake.

1429
01:45:27,030 --> 01:45:27,470
Mistake.

1430
01:45:32,790 --> 01:45:33,230
Boom.

1431
01:45:34,410 --> 01:45:35,150
There you are.

1432
01:45:36,750 --> 01:45:38,430
Hang out there for a moment, okay?

1433
01:45:39,550 --> 01:45:41,010
I'm gonna need to put a sign here.

1434
01:45:41,390 --> 01:45:42,310
If I have one.

1435
01:45:43,130 --> 01:45:44,170
Doesn't seem like I do.

1436
01:45:44,310 --> 01:45:44,550
I do.

1437
01:45:49,270 --> 01:45:55,650
Rescued villager here needs extra rescue.

1438
01:45:58,370 --> 01:46:00,110
Surely I'll find that later.

1439
01:46:01,490 --> 01:46:02,650
Where are you?

1440
01:46:05,190 --> 01:46:06,310
I hear you.

1441
01:46:08,590 --> 01:46:10,510
Are you upstairs or something?

1442
01:46:11,390 --> 01:46:11,670
Oh god.

1443
01:46:13,350 --> 01:46:14,050
Other pups!

1444
01:46:14,410 --> 01:46:16,090
One hit, one kill.

1445
01:46:21,840 --> 01:46:22,620
Don't explode.

1446
01:46:24,380 --> 01:46:25,580
ANOTHER ONE?!

1447
01:46:25,580 --> 01:46:30,340
Brother... I don't have enough for you.

1448
01:46:31,300 --> 01:46:31,960
You die.

1449
01:46:35,280 --> 01:46:36,840
You came at the wrong time, friend.

1450
01:46:47,130 --> 01:46:47,970
Sick jump.

1451
01:46:48,470 --> 01:46:49,150
Uh-oh.

1452
01:46:49,450 --> 01:46:50,230
Multiple bogeys!

1453
01:46:50,830 --> 01:46:52,470
I just realized I don't have a shield.

1454
01:46:57,190 --> 01:46:57,750
Jesus.

1455
01:46:59,770 --> 01:47:01,470
That guy's chest is missing.

1456
01:47:02,370 --> 01:47:04,150
I don't know how else to explain it, but look.

1457
01:47:07,730 --> 01:47:08,850
Wait, he's a skeleton.

1458
01:47:10,510 --> 01:47:11,370
That's normal.

1459
01:47:11,950 --> 01:47:14,090
It just looked really weird for a second.

1460
01:47:18,000 --> 01:47:18,880
Did you see that?

1461
01:47:19,200 --> 01:47:21,000
Okay, he despawned right in front of me.

1462
01:47:22,540 --> 01:47:23,880
I don't know how I feel about that.

1463
01:47:24,860 --> 01:47:26,220
Oh, he fell down, never mind.

1464
01:47:26,960 --> 01:47:28,140
I thought he despawned.

1465
01:47:34,000 --> 01:47:34,620
Hey, man.

1466
01:47:35,660 --> 01:47:37,120
Oh, yeah, there's so much dark here.

1467
01:47:37,200 --> 01:47:41,860
This is actually a prime candidate for trouble for the Orphan Crusher.

1468
01:47:51,970 --> 01:47:57,990
Yeah, this entire area has been insanely anti-Orphan Crusher.

1469
01:48:08,270 --> 01:48:09,670
God, that's actually amazing.

1470
01:48:09,910 --> 01:48:11,770
I love my new setup with the axe.

1471
01:48:13,250 --> 01:48:14,670
What a great decision.

1472
01:48:20,700 --> 01:48:23,700
Now I just need an enchantment that kills children.

1473
01:48:24,760 --> 01:48:25,660
Faster, I mean.

1474
01:48:28,310 --> 01:48:34,890
Well, I guess my current one does the job, but I feel like they're still too fast and too... I don't know.

1475
01:48:36,730 --> 01:48:38,150
You know, annoying.

1476
01:48:38,970 --> 01:48:40,570
I need an anti-that.

1477
01:48:41,250 --> 01:48:42,790
Whatever that is.

1478
01:48:44,270 --> 01:48:49,990
The essence of the child, you know, needs to be eradicated with an enchantment.

1479
01:48:53,310 --> 01:48:54,150
Oh god.

1480
01:49:01,520 --> 01:49:02,040
Here.

1481
01:49:02,040 --> 01:49:02,560
There.

1482
01:49:04,320 --> 01:49:05,980
Do an extra one, just in case.

1483
01:49:14,360 --> 01:49:14,880
Torch!

1484
01:49:17,380 --> 01:49:20,080
I think I may be slowly going insane from doing this.

1485
01:49:28,210 --> 01:49:29,450
Multiple spots here.

1486
01:49:32,370 --> 01:49:39,070
If there's anything I've learned is that these guys can spawn pretty much anywhere as long as there's no light.

1487
01:49:41,930 --> 01:49:45,490
So you really shouldn't take any chances with any type of terrain.

1488
01:49:46,990 --> 01:49:49,870
Life finds a way.

1489
01:49:54,650 --> 01:49:56,870
That actually makes me want to watch Jurassic Park again.

1490
01:49:57,330 --> 01:49:58,550
I haven't seen that in ages.

1491
01:49:59,690 --> 01:50:00,630
A classic.

1492
01:50:04,290 --> 01:50:04,790
Music.

1493
01:50:06,910 --> 01:50:07,410
Nothing.

1494
01:50:08,470 --> 01:50:09,570
I shall take it.

1495
01:50:13,970 --> 01:50:14,830
Almost hit the lava.

1496
01:50:15,130 --> 01:50:16,470
That was a bit risky for no reason.

1497
01:50:17,710 --> 01:50:18,450
Unnecessary risk.

1498
01:50:19,470 --> 01:50:20,490
See that guy down there?

1499
01:50:20,570 --> 01:50:21,430
He spawned in the darkness.

1500
01:50:21,730 --> 01:50:24,070
Just that little patch of darkness that I missed.

1501
01:50:26,350 --> 01:50:27,490
That'll teach me a lesson.

1502
01:50:30,030 --> 01:50:31,150
Not to miss darkness.

1503
01:50:47,620 --> 01:50:48,460
Can you feel it?

1504
01:50:48,580 --> 01:50:48,760
Listen.

1505
01:50:52,240 --> 01:50:53,540
No enemies.

1506
01:50:55,020 --> 01:51:00,600
These caves... are now the property... of me.

1507
01:51:01,340 --> 01:51:03,840
Except that little, uh, squadron down there.

1508
01:51:04,620 --> 01:51:06,780
Obviously we're gonna deal with that promptly.

1509
01:51:08,820 --> 01:51:11,420
We stifle all rebellions here.

1510
01:51:12,200 --> 01:51:13,960
No successionists allowed.

1511
01:51:14,560 --> 01:51:15,920
Everyone dies.

1512
01:51:17,280 --> 01:51:19,580
You either follow my rule...

1513
01:51:21,000 --> 01:51:21,800
Or you die.

1514
01:51:28,240 --> 01:51:30,040
I just want to make it clear, I'm not a king.

1515
01:51:31,700 --> 01:51:33,740
I am just a villager like everyone else.

1516
01:51:36,580 --> 01:51:39,960
Or just in the hypothetical case where if I would be a king, right?

1517
01:51:40,520 --> 01:51:41,520
What the f...

1518
01:51:54,220 --> 01:51:57,160
I was about to say, that looks like a bug, but look at the particle effect.

1519
01:51:59,840 --> 01:52:00,540
The hell?

1520
01:52:05,600 --> 01:52:06,000
Interesting.

1521
01:52:10,020 --> 01:52:11,060
I've never seen that?

1522
01:52:12,300 --> 01:52:17,860
Does the spider have some kind of innate fucking invisibility aspect to it?

1523
01:52:20,640 --> 01:52:23,280
Now that I think about it, did I ever try the silk?

1524
01:52:23,460 --> 01:52:24,900
The spider silk in a potion?

1525
01:52:30,580 --> 01:52:32,180
Maybe it's somehow related to the spiders.

1526
01:52:32,480 --> 01:52:33,300
Don't you dare!

1527
01:52:35,080 --> 01:52:35,600
Okay.

1528
01:52:36,000 --> 01:52:36,520
Good.

1529
01:52:42,260 --> 01:52:42,920
Above me?

1530
01:52:44,820 --> 01:52:45,800
No, in here, maybe.

1531
01:52:46,960 --> 01:52:48,160
I ran out of torches.

1532
01:52:51,540 --> 01:52:57,640
I think it's so cool that the shelter boxes can be attached to a wall.

1533
01:52:58,820 --> 01:52:59,760
Can I just say that?

1534
01:53:01,520 --> 01:53:03,080
That is such a good feature.

1535
01:53:05,930 --> 01:53:11,670
At least 50 liters... is what I require.

1536
01:53:14,650 --> 01:53:15,690
Blow up!

1537
01:53:15,750 --> 01:53:16,370
I'm dying!

1538
01:53:17,510 --> 01:53:18,310
Run!

1539
01:53:20,110 --> 01:53:21,610
I'm running into darkness!

1540
01:53:22,130 --> 01:53:24,170
The one place I swore to eradicate!

1541
01:53:24,410 --> 01:53:25,290
I'm dead.

1542
01:53:34,050 --> 01:53:34,970
Get out of my way!

1543
01:53:36,390 --> 01:53:37,270
I need a bucket!

1544
01:53:41,020 --> 01:53:41,860
Get out of there!

1545
01:53:43,200 --> 01:53:44,660
Wait, I can take the water, I guess.

1546
01:53:45,780 --> 01:53:46,400
You're free!

1547
01:53:48,500 --> 01:53:49,160
I'm going.

1548
01:53:49,720 --> 01:53:50,500
Straight back.

1549
01:53:51,000 --> 01:53:52,560
I have no idea where I died.

1550
01:53:52,680 --> 01:53:53,360
This is a problem.

1551
01:53:54,160 --> 01:53:55,960
This is a huge problem, actually.

1552
01:53:57,160 --> 01:54:00,140
I need to be fast... and precise.

1553
01:54:00,440 --> 01:54:00,960
Oh no!

1554
01:54:01,580 --> 01:54:02,300
It's night!

1555
01:54:04,540 --> 01:54:04,980
Fuck!

1556
01:54:06,780 --> 01:54:07,700
Okay, don't panic.

1557
01:54:07,800 --> 01:54:08,140
Don't panic.

1558
01:54:08,320 --> 01:54:08,760
It's fine.

1559
01:54:09,180 --> 01:54:11,180
Just walk around like this.

1560
01:54:13,100 --> 01:54:14,860
There's no use panicking.

1561
01:54:16,500 --> 01:54:17,940
Get up here slowly.

1562
01:54:18,900 --> 01:54:19,820
Find the spot.

1563
01:54:20,320 --> 01:54:21,140
Here it is.

1564
01:54:23,520 --> 01:54:25,540
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

1565
01:54:28,660 --> 01:54:29,140
Go.

1566
01:54:33,150 --> 01:54:34,070
Down, down, down.

1567
01:54:35,470 --> 01:54:40,250
Now... I do declare... Uh, this way?

1568
01:54:40,610 --> 01:54:41,570
No, the other way.

1569
01:54:41,810 --> 01:54:42,390
I think.

1570
01:54:43,730 --> 01:54:44,330
Over here.

1571
01:54:48,490 --> 01:54:49,790
Yep, this is it.

1572
01:54:52,730 --> 01:54:54,370
I know the approximate way.

1573
01:55:00,680 --> 01:55:01,920
We gotta go down here and left.

1574
01:55:07,920 --> 01:55:08,420
Watch this.

1575
01:55:11,840 --> 01:55:12,120
Sick!

1576
01:55:12,480 --> 01:55:18,000
I mean, there was no real risk there, because it was such a short distance, but you know, it was the idea of it.

1577
01:55:21,860 --> 01:55:23,100
Fuck, where did I die?

1578
01:55:28,640 --> 01:55:29,880
I have zero clue!

1579
01:55:30,660 --> 01:55:31,500
Oh no!

1580
01:55:41,320 --> 01:55:43,480
Wait, I... where was I?

1581
01:55:43,940 --> 01:55:44,900
Wait, where did I die?

1582
01:55:44,980 --> 01:55:45,480
Where did I die?

1583
01:55:47,640 --> 01:55:49,240
Where the fuck did I die?

1584
01:55:51,300 --> 01:55:52,020
Let me think.

1585
01:55:52,980 --> 01:55:54,180
Go towards darkness, I guess.

1586
01:55:56,880 --> 01:55:57,760
Did I die there?

1587
01:56:08,630 --> 01:56:16,050
I was fighting near... Pretty sure it was here.

1588
01:56:19,030 --> 01:56:20,210
I may have lost everything.

1589
01:56:21,950 --> 01:56:23,370
I have no idea where I died.

1590
01:56:23,990 --> 01:56:24,890
It's actually over.

1591
01:56:25,350 --> 01:56:26,290
My items are gone.

1592
01:56:31,010 --> 01:56:32,870
I have zero clue where I died.

1593
01:56:36,810 --> 01:56:37,290
Yep.

1594
01:56:37,910 --> 01:56:38,330
That was it.

1595
01:56:41,650 --> 01:56:42,430
Look around.

1596
01:56:53,390 --> 01:57:00,630
Uh... Could it have been... Wait, where did I... Where the hell did I die?

1597
01:57:11,380 --> 01:57:14,060
It could be anywhere down here, for all I know.

1598
01:57:19,900 --> 01:57:27,040
I don't see anything down here at all.

1599
01:57:32,840 --> 01:57:33,260
Okay, wait.

1600
01:57:33,380 --> 01:57:33,780
Sign there.

1601
01:57:36,300 --> 01:57:36,760
Oh, no.

1602
01:57:36,880 --> 01:57:37,860
I'm out of stamina.

1603
01:57:38,200 --> 01:57:38,860
Oh, no.

1604
01:57:40,220 --> 01:57:40,800
Wait, up there?

1605
01:57:42,540 --> 01:57:43,480
Actually, that could be it.

1606
01:57:43,800 --> 01:57:44,480
That could be it.

1607
01:57:51,260 --> 01:57:52,880
I would have gone towards the darkness, right?

1608
01:58:00,180 --> 01:58:01,080
Nah, it's over.

1609
01:58:01,760 --> 01:58:02,440
Items are gone.

1610
01:58:03,460 --> 01:58:04,720
I have no clue where I died.

1611
01:58:04,900 --> 01:58:05,100
Fuck.

1612
01:58:05,560 --> 01:58:06,600
That sucks, man.

1613
01:58:08,880 --> 01:58:10,240
That is really bad.

1614
01:58:11,220 --> 01:58:13,060
I can't even go up there because I have no weapons.

1615
01:58:17,720 --> 01:58:18,120
Shit.

1616
01:58:18,480 --> 01:58:18,600
Yeah.

1617
01:58:18,880 --> 01:58:20,240
I also fucked that one up just now.

1618
01:58:22,280 --> 01:58:22,680
Wait.

1619
01:58:24,300 --> 01:58:24,880
Oh, no.

1620
01:58:25,060 --> 01:58:25,180
Okay.

1621
01:58:30,310 --> 01:58:31,070
Where the hell?

1622
01:58:32,470 --> 01:58:33,270
Yeah, I don't know.

1623
01:58:37,090 --> 01:58:44,610
I feel like it's in a little cubby area that I died, but where exactly, I have no clue.

1624
01:58:46,410 --> 01:58:47,710
Wait, wasn't it up here, actually?

1625
01:58:54,490 --> 01:58:55,890
I remember being up here.

1626
01:58:59,430 --> 01:59:01,750
This was one of the last points that I lighted.

1627
01:59:07,630 --> 01:59:08,850
Did I go along here?

1628
01:59:13,340 --> 01:59:15,260
Wait a minute, this could be it.

1629
01:59:16,000 --> 01:59:16,960
Don't blow up on me.

1630
01:59:19,280 --> 01:59:19,800
Okay.

1631
01:59:20,660 --> 01:59:22,020
Wait, can I neutralize them with the water?

1632
01:59:22,600 --> 01:59:23,800
Oh, fuck the archer.

1633
01:59:25,340 --> 01:59:26,060
It's over.

1634
01:59:27,060 --> 01:59:28,400
Well, that's that.

1635
01:59:28,680 --> 01:59:29,420
That sucks.

1636
01:59:30,420 --> 01:59:32,160
Time to equip new armor and everything.

1637
01:59:32,840 --> 01:59:34,220
That is a real bummer.

1638
01:59:34,840 --> 01:59:36,440
I will never get that back.

1639
01:59:36,440 --> 01:59:37,840
I can tell you that right now.

1640
01:59:39,060 --> 01:59:40,280
That is not happening.

1641
01:59:42,520 --> 01:59:44,060
I have no good legs either.

1642
01:59:44,420 --> 01:59:45,620
So I'm just gonna take these.

1643
01:59:47,120 --> 01:59:48,040
Take those on.

1644
01:59:49,080 --> 01:59:51,340
I guess I could rock the trident.

1645
01:59:52,740 --> 01:59:54,020
That would be a way to do it.

1646
01:59:57,100 --> 01:59:58,040
Yeah, actually.

1647
01:59:59,680 --> 02:00:01,220
You know, good thing I found this bow.

1648
02:00:02,400 --> 02:00:04,400
Except it's about to be destroyed, so that sucks.

1649
02:00:09,180 --> 02:00:11,840
I feel like I should repair it, but I don't have any levels.

1650
02:00:12,380 --> 02:00:13,080
That's the problem.

1651
02:00:14,640 --> 02:00:15,260
Give me that.

1652
02:00:16,280 --> 02:00:17,520
Almost got a level from that.

1653
02:00:22,160 --> 02:00:22,680
Dang it.

1654
02:00:22,760 --> 02:00:23,180
Oh, you know what?

1655
02:00:23,200 --> 02:00:23,960
Let me check the thing.

1656
02:00:25,040 --> 02:00:26,500
We spent so much time down there.

1657
02:00:28,420 --> 02:00:30,300
Please give me good news here at least.

1658
02:00:30,580 --> 02:00:30,940
Please.

1659
02:00:32,320 --> 02:00:34,000
That does not be a sacrifice in vain.

1660
02:00:35,140 --> 02:00:35,440
Hey!

1661
02:00:39,020 --> 02:00:39,740
Respectable!

1662
02:00:39,740 --> 02:00:40,460
Hey?

1663
02:00:41,720 --> 02:00:43,020
Definitely improving?

1664
02:00:44,620 --> 02:00:45,920
Oh, my.

1665
02:00:46,360 --> 02:00:47,160
Look at that over there.

1666
02:00:50,110 --> 02:00:52,470
This is the one good thing about my existence right now.

1667
02:00:52,950 --> 02:00:53,650
My cows.

1668
02:00:54,130 --> 02:00:55,630
My cows bring me happiness!

1669
02:00:55,850 --> 02:00:56,670
Get away, Donovan!

1670
02:00:57,290 --> 02:00:58,230
You're not a cow.

1671
02:00:59,610 --> 02:01:00,730
I'm not gonna feed you.

1672
02:01:00,990 --> 02:01:02,310
It's not gonna be like last time.

1673
02:01:03,770 --> 02:01:04,630
Anyone else need?

1674
02:01:06,910 --> 02:01:09,350
Okay, I'm gonna leave them like this and let them multiply again.

1675
02:01:10,590 --> 02:01:12,710
I wanna see what the limit is on this.

1676
02:01:13,070 --> 02:01:15,290
How many cows can I fit in this one spot?

1677
02:01:16,850 --> 02:01:18,370
Yo, you need to get out of there, come on.

1678
02:01:18,990 --> 02:01:20,550
Why are they so obsessed with this?

1679
02:01:22,530 --> 02:01:23,370
Get out!

1680
02:01:26,820 --> 02:01:27,620
Donovan, come on.

1681
02:01:28,180 --> 02:01:29,300
Oh, you want to go out over here?

1682
02:01:29,460 --> 02:01:30,400
We can arrange that.

1683
02:01:33,480 --> 02:01:33,840
Here.

1684
02:01:34,180 --> 02:01:34,800
Cows, come here.

1685
02:01:36,280 --> 02:01:37,780
They're dragging him along, look.

1686
02:01:40,180 --> 02:01:41,280
Okay, nice, nice, nice.

1687
02:01:41,400 --> 02:01:41,940
Now I can do this.

1688
02:01:42,820 --> 02:01:43,180
Donovan!

1689
02:01:44,120 --> 02:01:45,720
Yeah, good job, good job, good job.

1690
02:01:45,800 --> 02:01:46,120
Teamwork.

1691
02:01:46,260 --> 02:01:46,520
High five.

1692
02:01:46,880 --> 02:01:47,420
High five.

1693
02:01:49,160 --> 02:01:49,520
Wonderful.

1694
02:01:50,200 --> 02:01:50,900
Back in you go.

1695
02:01:52,500 --> 02:01:54,200
Don... Oh...

1696
02:01:55,350 --> 02:01:59,150
Ho ho ho, you little bastard.

1697
02:02:00,450 --> 02:02:03,050
I see the issue here.

1698
02:02:04,410 --> 02:02:06,030
Nah, bro.

1699
02:02:08,050 --> 02:02:09,070
Nope.

1700
02:02:13,690 --> 02:02:15,990
Vulnerabilities detected and fixed.

1701
02:02:17,570 --> 02:02:18,910
Let's see you get in now.

1702
02:02:19,910 --> 02:02:20,810
Come on.

1703
02:02:22,430 --> 02:02:23,770
Oh, you can, huh?

1704
02:02:24,870 --> 02:02:25,950
Stupid Donovan.

1705
02:02:29,250 --> 02:02:29,990
There we go.

1706
02:02:30,230 --> 02:02:30,630
Fixed.

1707
02:02:34,030 --> 02:02:34,430
Okay.

1708
02:02:35,570 --> 02:02:35,970
Gunpowder.

1709
02:02:36,430 --> 02:02:37,070
In here.

1710
02:02:37,930 --> 02:02:38,330
Arrows.

1711
02:02:40,030 --> 02:02:43,630
Bro, I wonder if there's a way to somehow only make creepers.

1712
02:02:44,050 --> 02:02:45,570
And not have all the other craps.

1713
02:02:45,670 --> 02:02:46,910
Because I don't really care about arrows.

1714
02:02:47,510 --> 02:02:49,030
I only care about creepers.

1715
02:02:50,530 --> 02:02:51,810
Because I want that gunpowder.

1716
02:02:52,390 --> 02:02:53,910
And you know why I want the gunpowder?

1717
02:02:54,290 --> 02:02:55,510
It's not what you think it is.

1718
02:02:56,400 --> 02:02:57,720
You thought it was rockets?

1719
02:02:58,000 --> 02:02:58,500
You're wrong.

1720
02:02:58,960 --> 02:02:59,700
It's TNT.

1721
02:02:59,900 --> 02:03:05,280
That's why I require industrial-level production of gunpowder.

1722
02:03:05,720 --> 02:03:06,680
It's TNT, baby.

1723
02:03:07,960 --> 02:03:10,220
It's one of my favorite things in the game, and I need more of it.

1724
02:03:10,280 --> 02:03:12,080
I need to blow the world up.

1725
02:03:15,620 --> 02:03:18,620
My gear is actually kind of respectable, I would say, at this point.

1726
02:03:20,180 --> 02:03:21,080
Yeah, it's not bad.

1727
02:03:22,030 --> 02:03:23,910
In terms of weapons, I have a sword.

1728
02:03:24,290 --> 02:03:25,210
Let's see what I have up here.

1729
02:03:25,690 --> 02:03:26,690
What can I work with?

1730
02:03:26,810 --> 02:03:27,990
A mending pickaxe?

1731
02:03:29,670 --> 02:03:32,370
I mean, it's not really great, is it?

1732
02:03:33,670 --> 02:03:35,370
In fact, it's kind of shite.

1733
02:03:36,490 --> 02:03:39,750
Especially because in the beginning, I would rather have those levels for myself.

1734
02:03:41,870 --> 02:03:43,730
So, I don't know about that.

1735
02:03:45,390 --> 02:03:46,950
This is a pretty good axe.

1736
02:03:47,150 --> 02:03:47,770
I like that one.

1737
02:03:49,450 --> 02:03:49,850
Pickaxe?

1738
02:03:51,620 --> 02:03:52,620
Should I just take it?

1739
02:03:53,440 --> 02:03:56,300
Nah, I'm gonna make a standard diamond pickaxe.

1740
02:03:57,920 --> 02:04:00,900
We're raw-dogging the pickaxe, as they say.

1741
02:04:01,460 --> 02:04:02,300
Nobody says that.

1742
02:04:03,080 --> 02:04:04,700
But you know what I mean with it, right?

1743
02:04:05,380 --> 02:04:06,980
Now, let's just organize this a little bit.

1744
02:04:07,220 --> 02:04:09,380
Maybe I come back stronger than ever before!

1745
02:04:10,300 --> 02:04:11,740
Is it time for netherite?

1746
02:04:12,660 --> 02:04:15,640
Are we gonna come back with full netherite and prove our mettle?

1747
02:04:16,800 --> 02:04:17,980
What was I looking for just now?

1748
02:04:18,040 --> 02:04:18,300
I forgot.

1749
02:04:18,920 --> 02:04:19,800
Oh, yeah, diamonds.

1750
02:04:20,300 --> 02:04:20,640
Right.

1751
02:04:21,160 --> 02:04:22,220
Diamonds and sticks.

1752
02:04:22,680 --> 02:04:27,720
Put them together and... you are suddenly great at Minecraft.

1753
02:04:28,760 --> 02:04:30,320
Also, a shovel is what I need.

1754
02:04:31,640 --> 02:04:32,620
Uh, Donovan?

1755
02:04:37,260 --> 02:04:40,880
I just thought, didn't someone sell diamond armor?

1756
02:04:41,020 --> 02:04:41,780
That was kind of crazy.

1757
02:04:45,730 --> 02:04:46,430
Who was it?

1758
02:04:48,030 --> 02:04:48,430
Blacksmith.

1759
02:04:49,590 --> 02:04:51,230
I require your services.

1760
02:04:51,950 --> 02:04:52,350
Rosie!

1761
02:04:52,630 --> 02:04:53,210
Yeah, Rosie.

1762
02:04:54,010 --> 02:04:54,830
Erica's lost.

1763
02:04:55,150 --> 02:04:57,450
I can't find her and... Oh, my gear is red.

1764
02:04:58,790 --> 02:05:00,450
And when I say red, I mean it's gone.

1765
02:05:01,470 --> 02:05:03,790
It's a sad reality that we all have to face.

1766
02:05:03,950 --> 02:05:05,110
And when I say all, I mean me.

1767
02:05:05,510 --> 02:05:06,570
Just me, because I did it.

1768
02:05:06,870 --> 02:05:07,330
It was me.

1769
02:05:08,530 --> 02:05:10,750
Where's the rest of the population here?

1770
02:05:10,890 --> 02:05:11,930
Am I losing my mind?

1771
02:05:14,940 --> 02:05:15,500
Hello?

1772
02:05:15,960 --> 02:05:16,880
Oh, here we go.

1773
02:05:17,380 --> 02:05:18,580
There you are, Jaxter.

1774
02:05:18,900 --> 02:05:23,720
I'm gonna need to make... Ooh, that's really good.

1775
02:05:27,860 --> 02:05:28,420
Chessplate?

1776
02:05:29,980 --> 02:05:33,300
Aqua... Dude, you're actually kind of killing it.

1777
02:05:33,700 --> 02:05:34,880
I need those things.

1778
02:05:38,290 --> 02:05:39,290
I got money.

1779
02:05:40,410 --> 02:05:41,730
Let's see what I need the most.

1780
02:05:41,950 --> 02:05:42,550
Probably legs.

1781
02:05:43,370 --> 02:05:44,210
Hand them over.

1782
02:05:45,710 --> 02:05:46,270
Yeah.

1783
02:05:46,730 --> 02:05:48,670
And what about my current boots?

1784
02:05:49,570 --> 02:05:51,430
Chest plate is so-so.

1785
02:05:52,370 --> 02:05:53,490
Wait, why are you holding those?

1786
02:05:54,670 --> 02:05:58,250
What the... What does that mean?

1787
02:06:04,480 --> 02:06:05,900
Check that out.

1788
02:06:06,480 --> 02:06:10,880
If you hold money, they show you what they sell.

1789
02:06:13,300 --> 02:06:14,860
Can you believe that?

1790
02:06:16,620 --> 02:06:18,060
That's crazy to me.

1791
02:06:19,000 --> 02:06:24,960
In fact, that's two things I've discovered today where you hold an item and the world changes because of that.

1792
02:06:32,790 --> 02:06:33,470
Wait a minute!

1793
02:06:35,590 --> 02:06:37,010
Jaxter has an inventory!

1794
02:06:38,850 --> 02:06:42,750
Wait a minute, am I losing my mind, or is this UI completely different?

1795
02:06:44,630 --> 02:06:46,070
What is going on right now?

1796
02:06:46,170 --> 02:06:47,070
Wait a minute, am I losing my mind?

1797
02:06:50,440 --> 02:06:52,180
Oh, yeah, I'm losing my mind.

1798
02:06:54,020 --> 02:06:56,880
For some reason, I thought this was Jaxter's inventory?

1799
02:06:57,560 --> 02:06:59,020
I don't know what I was thinking, guys.

1800
02:06:59,140 --> 02:06:59,640
Holy crap.

1801
02:07:00,640 --> 02:07:01,700
I'm sorry about that.

1802
02:07:04,260 --> 02:07:06,000
I'm gonna need those emeralds.

1803
02:07:06,120 --> 02:07:06,380
Thank you.

1804
02:07:07,840 --> 02:07:08,660
Let's see the helmet.

1805
02:07:09,580 --> 02:07:10,460
Respiration and protection.

1806
02:07:10,460 --> 02:07:11,720
I actually adore that.

1807
02:07:12,680 --> 02:07:13,940
No need to change any of that.

1808
02:07:14,480 --> 02:07:16,860
The rest... I'm good.

1809
02:07:17,580 --> 02:07:18,380
Jaxter, you're up.

1810
02:07:18,480 --> 02:07:19,600
Wait, are you trapped there or something?

1811
02:07:22,560 --> 02:07:22,820
Go!

1812
02:07:24,380 --> 02:07:24,640
Oh!

1813
02:07:28,400 --> 02:07:29,200
Okay, you want to sleep.

1814
02:07:29,320 --> 02:07:29,520
You know what?

1815
02:07:29,560 --> 02:07:30,120
Let's go to sleep.

1816
02:07:30,880 --> 02:07:31,500
Let's go to sleep.

1817
02:07:32,540 --> 02:07:32,940
That's fine.

1818
02:07:37,520 --> 02:07:38,600
Well, crap.

1819
02:07:39,600 --> 02:07:44,240
Time to, well, get a bunch of new pouches, I guess.

1820
02:07:45,300 --> 02:07:46,560
Good thing I have some ready.

1821
02:07:46,720 --> 02:07:46,980
Food?

1822
02:07:48,500 --> 02:07:49,500
These are not named.

1823
02:07:50,700 --> 02:07:51,960
I require four.

1824
02:07:52,460 --> 02:07:53,560
It's the magic number.

1825
02:07:57,680 --> 02:07:58,440
There you go.

1826
02:07:59,680 --> 02:08:03,100
We're gonna need ten of these.

1827
02:08:06,040 --> 02:08:07,920
In the gray bundle, this is the mining one.

1828
02:08:08,720 --> 02:08:12,300
We're going to have a utility one, of course, that has one singular door.

1829
02:08:13,060 --> 02:08:17,320
It's going to have a... What was it?

1830
02:08:18,720 --> 02:08:19,820
I do not recall.

1831
02:08:22,720 --> 02:08:24,320
Definitely a bucket.

1832
02:08:24,600 --> 02:08:26,100
But I don't have a bucket right now.

1833
02:08:26,480 --> 02:08:29,200
They're all being used to transport axolotls.

1834
02:08:29,920 --> 02:08:30,840
But I can make one.

1835
02:08:32,640 --> 02:08:34,300
I believe it's simply...

1836
02:08:36,430 --> 02:08:37,070
Yeah.

1837
02:08:37,910 --> 02:08:38,710
Look at that.

1838
02:08:40,490 --> 02:08:41,510
In you go.

1839
02:08:43,150 --> 02:08:45,450
Compass is also something we require now.

1840
02:08:45,670 --> 02:08:46,290
Just one.

1841
02:08:47,050 --> 02:08:47,730
In there.

1842
02:08:49,190 --> 02:08:51,550
And a couple of leads.

1843
02:08:52,030 --> 02:08:52,550
Maybe three.

1844
02:08:53,710 --> 02:08:55,450
I could take more, I guess.

1845
02:08:57,070 --> 02:08:58,610
Let's take four at a time.

1846
02:09:01,450 --> 02:09:02,890
And... what else?

1847
02:09:04,300 --> 02:09:06,440
Thank god I still have my fishing rod, right?

1848
02:09:06,620 --> 02:09:07,620
Wait, do I have it?

1849
02:09:11,940 --> 02:09:13,320
That's not my good fishing rod.

1850
02:09:16,620 --> 02:09:17,000
Wait.

1851
02:09:22,000 --> 02:09:23,100
There's no way I lost that.

1852
02:09:25,980 --> 02:09:27,480
Did I take that with me?!

1853
02:09:27,480 --> 02:09:30,560
There's no way!

1854
02:09:34,530 --> 02:09:37,730
To be fair though, these two combined would be pretty good.

1855
02:09:39,990 --> 02:09:41,130
Hold on, am I blind?

1856
02:09:41,810 --> 02:09:45,310
I cannot see another fishing rod.

1857
02:09:47,390 --> 02:09:48,590
Did I put it in here?

1858
02:09:49,170 --> 02:09:50,010
I did!

1859
02:09:51,170 --> 02:09:51,710
Fantastic.

1860
02:09:52,510 --> 02:09:53,770
See, that was smart of me.

1861
02:09:54,970 --> 02:09:56,030
Good thing I did that.

1862
02:09:56,310 --> 02:09:57,050
I'm happy about that.

1863
02:09:57,490 --> 02:09:57,710
Good!

1864
02:09:58,190 --> 02:09:59,330
Armor, in.

1865
02:10:00,110 --> 02:10:01,750
Diamonds, in.

1866
02:10:02,290 --> 02:10:02,830
Door?

1867
02:10:03,760 --> 02:10:04,200
In.

1868
02:10:04,700 --> 02:10:05,880
This is the standard setup.

1869
02:10:06,660 --> 02:10:09,660
Also gonna need some work benches.

1870
02:10:10,700 --> 02:10:12,080
Ah, what's it called in this game?

1871
02:10:12,180 --> 02:10:15,020
It's called, uh... No.

1872
02:10:16,280 --> 02:10:16,720
Fuck!

1873
02:10:18,900 --> 02:10:19,840
I forgot how to do this.

1874
02:10:19,900 --> 02:10:21,200
Oh, is it just... Yeah, yeah, okay.

1875
02:10:22,540 --> 02:10:22,820
In.

1876
02:10:24,440 --> 02:10:25,140
There we go.

1877
02:10:25,260 --> 02:10:26,240
Take a little bit of this.

1878
02:10:26,500 --> 02:10:28,440
Put it in the, uh, this bundle.

1879
02:10:30,380 --> 02:10:30,820
Sticks.

1880
02:10:32,420 --> 02:10:37,580
We're gonna require just a bit of this to make torches.

1881
02:10:40,080 --> 02:10:40,580
Boom.

1882
02:10:41,580 --> 02:10:42,340
Torches there.

1883
02:10:44,060 --> 02:10:47,860
And ironically, I'm gonna be more armored now in the caves than I was before.

1884
02:10:48,540 --> 02:10:49,400
Isn't that funny?

1885
02:10:51,080 --> 02:10:53,100
Or maybe not, because I had a bunch of enchantments.

1886
02:10:53,200 --> 02:10:54,960
I'm not sure if I'm actually more armored now.

1887
02:10:55,940 --> 02:10:56,440
Maybe.

1888
02:10:59,430 --> 02:11:02,250
Also, I'm not gonna bring the... Am I gonna bring the triton?

1889
02:11:03,910 --> 02:11:04,730
I will bring it.

1890
02:11:05,050 --> 02:11:06,030
It's actually amazing.

1891
02:11:09,810 --> 02:11:11,530
Jaxter, I have more diamonds for you.

1892
02:11:15,130 --> 02:11:15,810
I have more.

1893
02:11:19,630 --> 02:11:20,730
Actually, not these.

1894
02:11:20,830 --> 02:11:21,190
Not these.

1895
02:11:21,510 --> 02:11:21,910
These.

1896
02:11:32,630 --> 02:11:33,110
Thanks.

1897
02:11:33,110 --> 02:11:33,950
In you go.

1898
02:11:34,270 --> 02:11:35,290
What else did you sell for me?

1899
02:11:36,390 --> 02:11:37,430
Look at those discounts!

1900
02:11:39,830 --> 02:11:41,190
By Kraphtar's hammer.

1901
02:11:42,390 --> 02:11:43,110
What a savings.

1902
