02:59:45,340 --> 02:59:46,480
I mean, I guess I have bone mule.

2723
02:59:47,660 --> 02:59:48,660
I could just use that.

2724
02:59:54,380 --> 02:59:55,300
Alright, come on.

2725
02:59:56,700 --> 02:59:57,380
Have you a fill.

2726
03:00:00,160 --> 03:00:00,920
Look at that.

2727
03:00:01,420 --> 03:00:01,540
Yeah.

2728
03:00:02,380 --> 03:00:03,040
Baby time.

2729
03:00:04,180 --> 03:00:05,280
Oh, put it back in the box.

2730
03:00:08,500 --> 03:00:09,560
I'm gonna have so many stakes.

2731
03:00:09,680 --> 03:00:10,440
I have 28 already.

2732
03:00:12,220 --> 03:00:13,780
And four in my inventory here.

2733
03:00:15,920 --> 03:00:20,160
Well, I don't... I'm not... I gotta say, the maze feels a little underwhelming here.

2734
03:00:20,620 --> 03:00:23,020
I mean, obviously there's a trick to it that I haven't discovered.

2735
03:00:25,140 --> 03:00:28,740
Like, why else would it be purple-colored or pink-colored, right?

2736
03:00:28,860 --> 03:00:32,540
This is totally... Oh, it does say six attack damage.

2737
03:00:36,520 --> 03:00:39,540
I mean, it's a decent amount of damage, I guess.

2738
03:00:39,840 --> 03:00:40,820
No, it's actually not.

2739
03:00:41,860 --> 03:00:45,780
The axe does more damage, and I think it reloads faster, even.

2740
03:00:48,440 --> 03:00:51,320
Yeah, I'm not sure about that.

2741
03:00:53,300 --> 03:00:53,780
Hmm.

2742
03:00:55,900 --> 03:00:57,220
I'm gonna experiment with that.

2743
03:00:57,240 --> 03:01:01,720
I'm just gonna have it on me and just fight with it and see if... maybe I get an idea.

2744
03:01:03,280 --> 03:01:03,760
Yeah.

2745
03:01:05,210 --> 03:01:06,470
Honestly, I'm not sure at this point.

2746
03:01:06,690 --> 03:01:08,810
Wind charge, that goes in there.

2747
03:01:09,270 --> 03:01:10,590
Let's just fix this up real quick.

2748
03:01:11,810 --> 03:01:12,830
All these books here.

2749
03:01:12,850 --> 03:01:14,650
I want to put looting on it, or something.

2750
03:01:15,730 --> 03:01:16,810
On my sword, I guess.

2751
03:01:17,090 --> 03:01:18,530
Oh wait, I have enough levels for that, I think.

2752
03:01:20,610 --> 03:01:21,530
This is a big one.

2753
03:01:22,690 --> 03:01:23,970
Oh, easy, easy!

2754
03:01:24,670 --> 03:01:25,070
Yes!

2755
03:01:26,310 --> 03:01:27,030
Much needed.

2756
03:01:28,350 --> 03:01:28,910
Very good.

2757
03:01:30,650 --> 03:01:31,710
Actually a huge upgrade.

2758
03:01:33,700 --> 03:01:35,540
N, N, N, N.

2759
03:01:40,040 --> 03:01:40,520
Yep.

2760
03:01:43,120 --> 03:01:43,980
What's up, Rosie?

2761
03:01:44,920 --> 03:01:46,080
Hope you're doing great.

2762
03:01:49,960 --> 03:01:51,000
Are you cooking, sir?

2763
03:01:51,700 --> 03:01:52,180
Jackster.

2764
03:01:56,760 --> 03:01:57,240
Okay.

2765
03:01:58,160 --> 03:01:59,020
That's gotta be it.

2766
03:02:02,050 --> 03:02:03,170
What a way to end though.

2767
03:02:03,390 --> 03:02:06,490
I thought everything was over and then at the last minute... BOOM!

2768
03:02:06,830 --> 03:02:07,850
We got the mace!

2769
03:02:24,500 --> 03:02:25,260
There we go.

2770
03:02:26,740 --> 03:02:28,540
I am not on a quesadilla break.

2771
03:02:28,660 --> 03:02:29,640
I had to disable that.

2772
03:02:32,380 --> 03:02:33,480
How about them apples?

2773
03:02:36,060 --> 03:02:37,980
Maze at the end, despite everything.

2774
03:02:41,440 --> 03:02:42,460
Past me died.

2775
03:02:43,240 --> 03:02:48,180
I sacrificed my elytra and all my other items so that Maze could walk.

2776
03:02:49,100 --> 03:02:49,760
You know?

2777
03:02:53,780 --> 03:02:54,700
It's a big deal.

2778
03:02:56,880 --> 03:03:01,140
I'm slowly unraveling the secrets of this game.

2779
03:03:04,120 --> 03:03:08,020
I gotta say though, I put down so many torches today, man.

2780
03:03:09,880 --> 03:03:13,300
There better be something good on the other side of this, I'm telling you.

2781
03:03:13,940 --> 03:03:20,520
I really hope I'm gonna live long enough and prosperous enough to see that day coming.

2782
03:03:26,080 --> 03:03:29,620
Oliver, this was my first stream after catching up on all the VODs.

2783
03:03:29,620 --> 03:03:30,440
Glad to have made it today.

2784
03:03:31,100 --> 03:03:32,440
Yeah, it's a long stream today.

2785
03:03:32,920 --> 03:03:34,060
The Friday special.

2786
03:03:42,470 --> 03:03:46,330
You can check the statistics to see how many torches you placed- OH SHIT, REALLY?!

2787
03:03:46,330 --> 03:03:48,410
I'm gonna do that.

2788
03:03:49,910 --> 03:03:50,930
But I just closed the game.

2789
03:03:52,570 --> 03:03:56,270
In fact, I wanna wait with that until I've placed all the torches I need to place.

2790
03:04:02,970 --> 03:04:04,390
You got me back into Minecraft.

2791
03:04:04,390 --> 03:04:04,870
Did I?

2792
03:04:05,930 --> 03:04:09,670
What kind of... Well, Minecraft are you playing?

2793
03:04:09,810 --> 03:04:11,970
Just the vanilla one, or are you playing with mods?

2794
03:04:12,470 --> 03:04:12,910
KM.

2795
03:04:17,750 --> 03:04:20,010
We're getting closer to partner plus level one.

2796
03:04:20,150 --> 03:04:20,750
I don't know what that is.

2797
03:04:20,870 --> 03:04:22,390
What is partner plus level one?

2798
03:04:23,470 --> 03:04:24,590
Can I actually do that?

2799
03:04:27,690 --> 03:04:28,350
Wait a minute.

2800
03:04:31,150 --> 03:04:32,390
How do I do that?

2801
03:04:33,790 --> 03:04:34,990
Wait, who said that?

2802
03:04:36,210 --> 03:04:36,870
AtlantCat.

2803
03:04:38,030 --> 03:04:39,790
Can you explain that, AtlantCat?

2804
03:04:42,450 --> 03:04:44,250
Partner plus level one.

2805
03:04:45,010 --> 03:04:46,090
Plus program.

2806
03:04:49,390 --> 03:04:50,670
Oh, shit!

2807
03:04:56,350 --> 03:04:57,110
Oh!

2808
03:05:01,380 --> 03:05:02,240
Oh, yeah?

2809
03:05:03,040 --> 03:05:05,980
Wait, uh... Plus points.

2810
03:05:06,900 --> 03:05:08,740
Okay, I need to look into that.

2811
03:05:08,920 --> 03:05:09,920
That's apparently a thing.

2812
03:05:10,300 --> 03:05:13,380
And I think I may need to do something to actually activate it.

2813
03:05:15,780 --> 03:05:17,420
I need to make a bag of my world.

2814
03:05:18,480 --> 03:05:21,340
It means you get 60-40 split instead of... That would be amazing.

2815
03:05:24,300 --> 03:05:25,520
Yeah, that would be crazy.

2816
03:05:27,060 --> 03:05:28,620
It shows it below the stream.

2817
03:05:31,460 --> 03:05:32,060
Does it?

2818
03:05:35,560 --> 03:05:39,340
God, I feel like... I actually feel like a grandma right now with technology.

2819
03:05:42,580 --> 03:05:51,740
Like, I know everything there is to know about YouTube, everything about that interface and everything associated with it, but Twitch is still like... There's so many things with Twitch, it's insane.

2820
03:05:54,960 --> 03:05:56,200
Herobrine is in your world?

2821
03:05:56,300 --> 03:05:58,260
I don't know what that means, OnanHuma.

2822
03:05:59,640 --> 03:06:00,860
Are you spoilering?

2823
03:06:01,280 --> 03:06:03,180
Or saying something you shouldn't?

2824
03:06:04,180 --> 03:06:06,440
For me, it does if I'm not in theater mode.

2825
03:06:07,400 --> 03:06:08,120
Your world is haunted?

2826
03:06:08,220 --> 03:06:08,920
That's what I'm saying!

2827
03:06:09,040 --> 03:06:09,460
It's cursed!

2828
03:06:10,030 --> 03:06:10,870
I told you.

2829
03:06:13,070 --> 03:06:15,210
Are you considering selling merch at some point?

2830
03:06:15,310 --> 03:06:16,350
I would definitely buy some.

2831
03:06:16,750 --> 03:06:17,510
Honestly, no.

2832
03:06:19,010 --> 03:06:20,090
Think about it like this.

2833
03:06:20,210 --> 03:06:24,490
If I were to ask you, Gonch, are you considering selling merch anytime soon?

2834
03:06:25,450 --> 03:06:28,270
The way you're feeling right now is how I'm feeling right now.

2835
03:06:30,130 --> 03:06:31,270
Like, what would I sell?

2836
03:06:32,530 --> 03:06:33,870
I don't have any merch to sell.

2837
03:06:33,970 --> 03:06:34,890
I don't know how to make things.

2838
03:06:34,890 --> 03:06:37,030
I don't know anything about merch.

2839
03:06:38,070 --> 03:06:40,530
Also, I can't imagine that people would actually buy it.

2840
03:06:40,610 --> 03:06:48,030
I mean, you say you would, but... The idea of selling merch is like... We're not there yet, you know what I mean?

2841
03:06:50,670 --> 03:06:52,330
Oh, the style is dead t-shirt?

2842
03:06:52,470 --> 03:06:53,450
That could be a thing, yeah.

2843
03:06:54,250 --> 03:06:56,570
Okay, that one is actually a pretty good idea.

2844
03:06:57,710 --> 03:07:04,550
But other than that, I can't really see anything that is like... You know, my friend sent me a...

2845
03:07:06,200 --> 03:07:08,040
My friend is actually gonna buy me t-shirts.

2846
03:07:08,920 --> 03:07:10,480
One of them is called... let me find it here.

2847
03:07:11,180 --> 03:07:12,220
Made me laugh so much.

2848
03:07:14,540 --> 03:07:16,580
Biggest slut in the Taco Bell Cantina.

2849
03:07:17,680 --> 03:07:19,540
You can probably Google that and find a t-shirt.

2850
03:07:19,680 --> 03:07:20,520
I want that t-shirt.

2851
03:07:20,620 --> 03:07:25,620
There's also another one with like a picture of... of a pear.

2852
03:07:26,040 --> 03:07:28,340
And it says, I eat pears and shit like that.

2853
03:07:28,740 --> 03:07:30,100
Shout out to all the pear.

2854
03:07:31,960 --> 03:07:33,620
I don't know, it's just funny to me.

2855
03:07:34,380 --> 03:07:35,520
I want that shit.

2856
03:07:37,800 --> 03:07:39,180
EDP shirt, essentially.

2857
03:07:39,540 --> 03:07:41,140
Actually, yeah, that would be a good one.

2858
03:07:41,260 --> 03:07:41,960
I would wear that.

2859
03:07:42,980 --> 03:07:44,180
What would it look like, though?

2860
03:07:49,060 --> 03:07:49,660
Hold on.

2861
03:07:54,120 --> 03:07:55,280
Let me try something here.

2862
03:07:59,750 --> 03:08:01,330
There we go.

2863
03:08:03,050 --> 03:08:04,150
There we go.

2864
03:08:05,610 --> 03:08:06,450
Like that.

2865
03:08:32,330 --> 03:08:33,410
Oh no, what's wrong?

2866
03:08:34,050 --> 03:08:35,050
It doesn't work!

2867
03:08:36,910 --> 03:08:41,530
I don't know what's going on with that.

2868
03:08:42,610 --> 03:08:43,590
It doesn't work.

2869
03:08:45,510 --> 03:08:47,090
I tried to do a paint thing.

2870
03:08:47,510 --> 03:08:50,070
I was gonna design the merch right now.

2871
03:08:51,230 --> 03:08:52,530
Don't know why it doesn't work.

2872
03:08:54,130 --> 03:08:55,350
Maybe paint is bugged.

2873
03:08:56,710 --> 03:08:59,430
But I was gonna make, like, um...

2874
03:08:59,500 --> 03:09:05,420
You know, some dirt blocks, and then you have the 3x3 dirt block above that, you know?

2875
03:09:05,560 --> 03:09:06,460
And then the words EDP.

2876
03:09:06,620 --> 03:09:07,880
That could be kind of funny, honestly.

2877
03:09:08,240 --> 03:09:09,040
I like that.

2878
03:09:09,960 --> 03:09:10,660
Paint is dead.

2879
03:09:23,370 --> 03:09:27,370
Okay, you guys have some pretty good ideas, actually.

2880
03:09:29,990 --> 03:09:31,430
What about a demon t-shirt?

2881
03:09:31,650 --> 03:09:32,910
I know you guys love that meme.

2882
03:09:35,070 --> 03:09:36,410
What would it look like, though?

2883
03:09:37,790 --> 03:09:42,210
Would it just be like a drawn finger or a hand with the finger sticking out?

2884
03:09:48,760 --> 03:09:49,720
Oh my god.

2885
03:09:55,700 --> 03:09:57,800
ODB and diorite are requirement merch.

2886
03:09:58,140 --> 03:10:01,840
But it feels so low effort to put a diorite on a t-shirt.

2887
03:10:03,580 --> 03:10:07,560
If anything, there would have to be a lot of effort in there, you know, to make it look cool, I think.

2888
03:10:10,220 --> 03:10:11,080
The gym button.

2889
03:10:11,240 --> 03:10:12,560
But isn't that already a merch?

2890
03:10:12,660 --> 03:10:16,220
I can imagine that already being a merch for the Stanley Parable.

2891
03:10:16,830 --> 03:10:18,430
In fact, you can buy a button.

2892
03:10:18,790 --> 03:10:21,130
Like a physical button in real life.

2893
03:10:21,130 --> 03:10:22,290
When you press it, it says Jim.

2894
03:10:24,390 --> 03:10:25,630
I actually want to buy that.

2895
03:10:30,990 --> 03:10:32,550
Diorite is boring and not unique.

2896
03:10:32,710 --> 03:10:34,690
Lots of YouTubers already use Diorite as their joke.

2897
03:10:34,890 --> 03:10:36,490
Is Diorite a common joke?

2898
03:10:36,830 --> 03:10:42,090
Did I actually accidentally somehow fall into that same joke?

2899
03:10:42,890 --> 03:10:43,990
That's insane.

2900
03:10:44,290 --> 03:10:45,030
Why is it a joke?

2901
03:10:46,590 --> 03:10:49,690
Why do people think Diorite is a joke?

2902
03:10:50,410 --> 03:10:51,730
It's a jokey block?

2903
03:10:53,710 --> 03:10:54,630
What do you mean?

2904
03:10:55,870 --> 03:10:56,830
What does that mean?

2905
03:10:58,760 --> 03:11:02,420
It's a joke as... It's a joke as bird poop.

2906
03:11:04,140 --> 03:11:05,260
Because it's ugly?

2907
03:11:07,040 --> 03:11:09,040
Yeah, it is ugly, actually.

2908
03:11:09,160 --> 03:11:09,440
You're right.

2909
03:11:10,420 --> 03:11:11,880
It looks like skeletons.

2910
03:11:12,420 --> 03:11:13,780
And I hate skeletons.

2911
03:11:17,470 --> 03:11:19,390
Some people hate it, some people love it.

2912
03:11:19,610 --> 03:11:20,630
It's more about the looks.

2913
03:11:23,190 --> 03:11:26,930
Yeah, you know, now that I think about it, I don't like the way diorite looks.

2914
03:11:29,050 --> 03:11:30,050
I think I hate it.

2915
03:11:30,450 --> 03:11:31,490
I'm in the hate camp.

2916
03:11:33,230 --> 03:11:34,750
Like, when would you ever use that?

2917
03:11:37,590 --> 03:11:39,010
It's the birch of stone.

2918
03:11:39,890 --> 03:11:41,710
That's a good way of putting it.

2919
03:11:42,890 --> 03:11:44,590
I mean, I don't know if I like birch either.

2920
03:11:49,680 --> 03:11:52,260
Using it for pillars in my town hall heart.

2921
03:11:54,600 --> 03:12:04,200
Well, as long as you find enjoyment in Diorite, far be it from me to get in the way of extracting fun from Diorite.

2922
03:12:05,940 --> 03:12:07,500
I'm at my peak merchandise.

2923
03:12:07,980 --> 03:12:09,300
I don't say that that often.

2924
03:12:09,400 --> 03:12:09,680
Do I?

2925
03:12:09,840 --> 03:12:11,720
I said it once or twice.

2926
03:12:12,080 --> 03:12:15,320
I think Diego, who was in the chat, used to say that a lot.

2927
03:12:20,140 --> 03:12:22,260
But I have peaked quite a bit.

2928
03:12:22,380 --> 03:12:28,080
Today was unfortunately, I would say, a pretty flat curve.

2929
03:12:28,460 --> 03:12:30,020
Then it took a nose dive.

2930
03:12:30,460 --> 03:12:34,220
And then after that, I got picked up by a bird.

2931
03:12:34,400 --> 03:12:35,980
And I got swooped up into the heavens.

2932
03:12:37,820 --> 03:12:39,340
The maze, of course.

2933
03:12:40,980 --> 03:12:43,880
That's so demon could work as a sticker just pointing at nothing.

2934
03:12:48,160 --> 03:12:50,380
What the fuck is this little archaeologist?

2935
03:12:51,200 --> 03:12:51,980
Where's that from?

2936
03:12:52,140 --> 03:12:53,540
I feel like I've heard that before, Dioplia.

2937
03:12:58,260 --> 03:13:01,000
You walked around for so long with the heavy core in your inventory?

2938
03:13:01,240 --> 03:13:02,220
Oh no, did I?

2939
03:13:04,320 --> 03:13:06,920
By the way, something completely unrelated.

2940
03:13:07,420 --> 03:13:11,180
For those that are following the Elden Ring streams, I did actually check out the VOD.

2941
03:13:11,480 --> 03:13:13,660
And I saw how many souls I lost.

2942
03:13:14,240 --> 03:13:15,320
And I died inside.

2943
03:13:15,900 --> 03:13:18,260
I realized I should not have checked.

2944
03:13:20,040 --> 03:13:23,180
I... Man, I was devastated when I sat there and looked at that.

2945
03:13:23,940 --> 03:13:25,200
Because I was so sure.

2946
03:13:26,660 --> 03:13:29,280
That I only lost like 10k max.

2947
03:13:30,140 --> 03:13:32,040
And yeah, I should not have looked.

2948
03:13:33,040 --> 03:13:34,680
Ignorance is bliss sometimes, guys.

2949
03:13:43,460 --> 03:13:45,900
I guess I had runes from last time I played, yeah.

2950
03:13:48,040 --> 03:13:52,540
We thought you were trolling because you said you had nothing valuable on you, didn't care if you died when you had the heavy core.

2951
03:13:56,140 --> 03:13:56,900
That's amazing.

2952
03:13:58,460 --> 03:13:59,820
I mean, think about it like this.

2953
03:13:59,960 --> 03:14:03,280
If I actually died and didn't come back for it, I wouldn't have known better.

2954
03:14:03,460 --> 03:14:04,840
Once again, ignorance is bliss.

2955
03:14:08,610 --> 03:14:09,210
Rip, man.

2956
03:14:09,410 --> 03:14:09,570
Rip.

2957
03:14:10,170 --> 03:14:10,830
Bye-bye, Oliver.

2958
03:14:11,110 --> 03:14:11,810
See ya, Glorkish.

2959
03:14:12,190 --> 03:14:12,890
Nice to have you.

2960
03:14:15,110 --> 03:14:17,210
The chat went crazy when you found the heavy core.

2961
03:14:17,890 --> 03:14:19,830
How the fuck did you guys see that so fast?

2962
03:14:20,490 --> 03:14:27,370
Because I looked at the things that came out of the... thing, and I didn't see that, and I guess I didn't check what I picked up when I killed people.

2963
03:14:29,290 --> 03:14:29,990
Yeah, I don't know.

2964
03:14:30,710 --> 03:14:32,910
Anyway... Guys, that was a long-ass stream.

2965
03:14:33,390 --> 03:14:34,210
Almost eight hours.

2966
03:14:36,470 --> 03:14:37,510
I hope you enjoyed that.

2967
03:14:37,710 --> 03:14:40,350
I'm actually gonna split it up into two parts and put them on YouTube.

2968
03:14:40,930 --> 03:14:46,210
Just because eight hours is a bit intimidating of a VOD to just smack on YouTube like that.

2969
03:14:46,610 --> 03:14:47,250
I think.

2970
03:14:48,390 --> 03:14:51,550
I'm probably gonna cut the brick right when I eat my chinchilla.

2971
03:14:51,730 --> 03:14:52,310
I mean, wait.

2972
03:14:53,610 --> 03:14:54,690
Not a chinchilla.

2973
03:14:54,770 --> 03:14:55,230
What's it called?

2974
03:14:55,410 --> 03:14:56,130
